Odin 3 Qualcomm Sensor Core data

The sensor registry inputs in this directory were recovered from the stock
Odin 3 Android BSP. They select the CQ8725S/Pakala QMI8658 profile while
leaving calibration state writable and persistent under /userdata.

Stock ADSP firmware revision: LPAIDSP.HT.1.1-01147.1-PAKALA-1
SoC ID: 706

Runtime path
------------

The ADSP/QSH firmware owns the QMI8658. hexagonrpcd exposes the QSH file
services, libqmi/libssc receives SSC reports over QRTR, and ssccli provides a
raw accelerometer/gyroscope smoke test. The generated registry and learned
per-unit calibration live under /userdata/system/qcom-sensors/odin3 and are
never overwritten automatically.

Run `batocera-qcom-sensors-test 5` on an Odin 3 to validate both streams.

Future emulator attachment points
---------------------------------

Batocera continues to use evmapy for its normal controller mapping. No input
daemon or emulator hook is enabled by this bring-up.

The least invasive follow-up is a launch-scoped libssc bridge with two optional
outputs:

* DSU/Cemuhook UDP on localhost for Cemu and Azahar. Their motion source is
  separate from their normal SDL button source, so evmapy need not be replaced.
* A uinput motion-only device with INPUT_PROP_ACCELEROMETER, ABS_X/Y/Z for
  acceleration and ABS_RX/RY/RZ for angular velocity. RPCS3 already accepts a
  separate evdev "buddy device" and Dolphin has equivalent evdev motion maps.

Configgen should start that bridge only for a motion-enabled game, configure
the corresponding motion source, and stop the bridge on emulator exit.
